Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_dirread.c
Line: 2697
Function: TIFFReadDirEntrySlong8Array
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: Allocates data with size count * 8 without checking for size_t overflow. On 32-bit platforms this can wrap to a too-small allocation. The subsequent conversion loops write count 64-bit elements into data (e.g., at lines 2712–2724, 2733–2739, 2748–2754, 2763–2769, 2778–2784), leading to heap buffer overflow when count is large.

